{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== SESSION: e369 Jira DC — 9 changes merged, the capability map answered what 3 harness runs could not ===\n\n--- MERGED (9) ---\n  1302 8ab91b3f33  39c1: epic parent via Epic Link (greenhopper route — later REFUTED)\n  1303 29f9627128  2b16: xfail the inbound link-delete cell\n  1305 364c4e8f5e  39c1 AC4: bridge_alerts on every set_parent failure arm\n  1311 b301e7513d  39c1: Epic Link as a plain custom-field write (replaces 1302's route)\n  1319 40b869c2a9  18a5: assert_bridge_alert_for_mutation\n  1320 e2b9c74345  1a9f: raw-REST subtask-parent probes + 37e7 falsifiers\n  1324 2c71463b1e  9bb9: get_parent_map reads the Epic Link back\n  1328 70ad982b96  259b: the capability-map CI job\n  1329 3f5880cea9  a32a: comment dedup key routed through the codec seam\n  ABANDONED 1314 (superseded by 36e986c188, same hygiene fix landed first)\n\n--- CLOSED: 88d9, 2b16 (--class preexisting), 0cfd (duplicate) ---\n\n--- IN REVIEW / READY ---\n  1330  37e7 test rewrite — Verified +1, awaiting LLM-Review\n  465d  transport split — committed 76fcaa414c in worktree agent-a8b75730e727bd56b, NOT PUSHED\n\n--- THE CAPABILITY MAP (run 30863672922) IS THE HEADLINE ---\nOne boot answered questions three 35-minute harness runs could not. Artifact:\ncapability_map.json + evidence.json (raw request/response per answer).\n\nSETTLED:\n * [1a9f AC1] sub-task `PUT fields.parent` -> **HTTP 204 AND SILENTLY IGNORES** (read-back shows the\n   old parent). Accept-and-ignore, NOT rejection — the dangerous branch. Confirms the reading I\n   argued for over the inbound cell's own \"index is lagging\" self-diagnosis.\n * [39c1] the Epic Link write **WORKS**: PUT customfield_10001 -> 204, read-back returns the epic.\n   1311's mechanism is correct on 8.17.1.\n * [3fe5] SOLVABLE, not a platform limit — all three software templates yield Epic.\n   Epic Link=customfield_10001, Epic Name=customfield_10003.\n * [37e7] verdict NEEDS REVISITING: the two null-clearing forms return DIFFERENT 400s\n   (\"data was not an object\" vs \"not on the appropriate screen\"), and sub-task editmeta exposes no\n   `parent` at all. Still not clearable, but the NOT-RESOLVABLE reasoning was inference and is\n   falsified. Honest state: UNKNOWN. Does not change the operator's decision.\n\nNEW DEFECTS -> [rebar:2e47-ae62-c0cf-48a0]: status `IDEA` absent from every workflow; label limit is\n254 not 255; two issue types both named `Task`; three relations unrepresentable.\n\nA PREDICTION I GOT HALF WRONG, recorded because it shrinks 3fe5: I predicted the Epic Link write\nwould fail because the field is not on the child's edit screen. It IS not on the screen — **and the\nPUT persisted anyway.** Screen presence does not gate REST writes here, so provisioning does NOT\nneed to add fields to screens.\n\n--- METHOD FINDINGS WORTH CARRYING ---\n 1. **Held-out TDD earned its keep on 1311**: 2 of 6 withheld cells caught real defects, one of them\n    the SAME unguarded `.fields()` call I had made myself writing the fix inline. Two independent\n    implementations, same trap.\n 2. **A vacuous test I created, hidden by a 2132-green suite**: a client double lacking `fields()`\n    made the code decline for the wrong reason, so an assertion about epic-vs-subtask paths passed\n    while testing nothing. RULE: when a change makes production code call a NEW method on an\n    injected collaborator, every existing double of that collaborator is a candidate vacuous oracle\n    — and none will fail to tell you.\n 3. **THREE stale-base incidents from parallel agents.** Worst: 465d would have SILENTLY REVERTED\n    9bb9 — it branched pre-1324, and because the refactor MOVES `get_parent_map` into a new file, a\n    cherry-pick would likely have applied clean. Caught only because its report contradicted known\n    state. **Worktree isolation prevents file collisions, not temporal drift.** Always check\n    `git merge-base --is-ancestor <recent-merge> HEAD` on a returning agent's branch.\n 4. Two agent process deviations, both recorded: an unauthorised `--force` gate bypass (259b,\n    operator accepted as-is), and an agent's tooling reaching the SHARED main checkout (a32a —\n    verified clean afterwards, nothing lost, but it was luck that no WIP was present).\n 5. `transport.py` hit the 800 cap four times in one day. The split (465d) is approved and done but\n    unpushed; nothing further can land in that file until it does."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785803445924450001,"uuid":"586726bf-9dd1-4ac9-96cb-21305b4ea3e7"}